*How it will be measured.* The test set holds << num(ev.single_fault_cases, 0) >> single-fault units (<< ev.channel_strip_cases >> on the channel strip, << ev.cases_per_block >> per block), seeds disjoint from training. Each case draws a fault uniformly from the catalog and keeps the unit only if it shows a symptom, else draws another fault, so faults count by how often they cause a symptom, not how often they fail; old electrolytics and tubes fail far more often than film resistors, so T14 also reweights to a capacitor-heavy mix. Complaints come from a phrase bank the reader was not developed on (its overall score was seen once, before the rules last changed; T18 uses a sealed second bank), in three voices, never name a part, and drop each symptom with probability << m('library.complaint_noise.p_omit_pct') | round | int >>% and add each other symptom with << m('library.complaint_noise.p_add_pct') | round | int >>%. Stress sets: << ev.unmodeled_cases >> units outside the catalog (70% double faults, 30% a wrong-value part or a solder bridge); << ev.aged_cases >> aged units (electrolytics up to << m('library.aging.electrolytic_c_loss_max_pct') | round | int >>% low with up to << m('library.aging.electrolytic_esr_max_x') | round | int >>× their series resistance, resistors up to << m('library.aging.resistor_drift_max_pct') | round | int >>% high, tubes up to << m('library.aging.triode_emission_loss_max_pct') | round | int >>% weaker); tolerances 1.5, 2 and 3 times wider. The scripts, both engines and the full system (@tab:methods) diagnose every unit; the scripts share the engine's inference and stopping rule and unsolder their leading suspect at << pct(m('library.design.confirm_at'), 0) >> belief, so each margin isolates how measurements are chosen. A language model works alone, and with our simulator as a tool (no bar), on a stratified << ev.llm_subset >>-unit subset with the same information, three sessions per unit.

*Hardware and people.* For T7 a teammate who does not record inserts << ev.fault_board_min >> faults, in a sealed random order, into three 24 V driver boards (one of used parts); each test point is read once per fault and every method replayed on the recordings. Study S1 (pre-registered, no bar) will time at least six technicians with and without the tool, after ethics review.

*Pilots set the bars; no test unit has been run.* Bars come from a pilot on units simulated for it alone (<< m('pilot2.n_cases.channel_strip') >> channel strip, << m('pilot2.n_cases.driver') >> per block, << m('bars.targets.T13.n_pilot') | int >> out-of-model, << m('bars.targets.T6.n_pilot') | int >> aged), after two earlier pilots exposed problems since fixed. Weighted like the test set (channel strip one half, each block one tenth), the full system named the right group first on << pct(m('bars.targets.T1.estimate'), 1) >> of pilot units, naming a group on << pct(m('bars.targets.T23.estimate'), 1) >> and right on << pct(m('bars.targets.T23.accuracy_estimate'), 1) >> of those. The engine alone, ignoring the complaint, was right on << pct(m('bars.context.accuracy_weighted.engine'), 1) >>: the noisy complaints saved << num(m('bars.context.complaint_effort_saving_pct'), 1) >>% of the effort but cost << num(-m('bars.context.complaint_accuracy_change_pts'), 1) >> points of accuracy, so the complaint reader has yet to prove itself (T11, T18). On the channel strip the engine alone was right on << pct(m('bars.context.cs_top1.engine'), 1) >> at a mean effort of << num(m('bars.context.cs_mean_effort.engine'), 1) >>, half-split tracing on << pct(m('bars.context.cs_top1.half_split'), 1) >> at << num(m('bars.context.cs_mean_effort.half_split'), 1) >>, the chart on << pct(m('bars.context.cs_top1.fixed_order'), 1) >> at << num(m('bars.context.cs_mean_effort.fixed_order'), 1) >> and random probing on << pct(m('bars.context.cs_top1.random'), 1) >> at << num(m('bars.context.cs_mean_effort.random'), 1) >>. Each bar is the pilot estimate moved << m('bars.k') >> standard errors against the system and rounded; because the confidence bound must clear it, a primary can be missed even if the system matches the pilot, and a miss will be reported as one.

*Scope.* In: single static faults (opens, shorts, drift, wear) and the hum and distortion they cause, in supplies, preamplifier and line-level stages. Out: power amplifiers (another catalog), intermittent and mechanical faults (static simulation cannot produce them), double faults (flagged only), mains-side work, units without a schematic, unattended probing.

#decision("Score by ambiguity group and weighted effort")[
*Options:* per-part accuracy and a count of measurements, or group accuracy and weighted effort. *Choice:* the latter: per-part scoring rewards lucky guesses between faults with identical readings, and unsoldering a part is not like touching a probe. *Consequence:* group sizes are reported (@tab:library) and effort targets use weighted units.
]

<< part(4, "Preliminary AI approach, risks and ethics") >>

*Why a hybrid.* Language models guess when uncertain, partly because training and evaluation reward guessing << cite('kalai_why_hallucinate_2025') >>; the 97.59% system in << P1 >> needed a simulation check. Simulation supplies the physics; Bayesian inference keeps a probability for every suspect, "no single fault fits" included, updated after each reading through likelihoods learned from the simulated units: one to three Gaussians per fault over the circuit's readings (<< cs.spice_observables >> on the channel strip, << m('library.circuits.channel_strip.observables_by_kind.dc') >> of them DC voltages), with boosted trees << cite('ke_2017_lightgbm') >> as a comparison engine (weighted pilot top-1: << pct(m('bars.context.accuracy_weighted.engine'), 1) >> and << pct(m('bars.context.engine_disc_top1_weighted'), 1) >>). The next measurement maximizes expected information gain per unit of effort, as in sequential fault diagnosis << cite('pattipati_alexandridis_1990') >>; a diagnosis stops at << pct(m('library.design.stop_threshold'), 0) >> belief in one group, at the budget, or when nothing informative remains. The language model reads complaints (offline, a rule-based reader does), proposes meter-photo readings for confirmation and explains each step; every number it writes must trace to a reading (T17). It stays only if T5, T18 and T19 show it helps.

#figure(
  placement: auto,
  table(
    columns: (1.1fr, 2.9fr, 0.9fr),
    table.header([Method], [Chooses the next measurement], [Role]),
    [Fixed-order chart], [A textbook chart's order: supplies, output, signal, DC, hum, response], [Baseline],
    [Half-split tracing], [Supplies; halve the signal path with a tone; DC at the first bad stage], [Expert baseline],
    [Random probing], [Any unmeasured point; never unsolders], [Floor],
